summary:
  The Playing page's big button wears the Stop face over an episode or a My
  Music file, although its press pauses and keeps the place.

history:
  The button's glyph and name asked only whether a timeshift buffer was
  ready. When 2026.44 made its press keep an episode, the face went on
  saying Stop for a day: it promised an end and delivered a pause. The face
  is asked of the facts the press is answered from, and a press that keeps
  something is a Pause.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TransportLogic.js

find:
      if (act === "keep") return "pause";

replace:
      if (act === "keep") return "stop";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_an_episode_or_a_file_that_plays_wears_the_pause_face
  and tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_for_every_state_the_face_is_what_a_press_does,
  and by tests/qml/tst_transportroads.qml::test_the_face_and_the_desk_say_the_same_thing_along_the_way.
  Line-neutral.
